[00:37.33] Dakota and Nebraska to the lazy Rio Grande
[00:44.17] It fell across our city like a curtain of black rolled down
[00:50.81] We thought it was our judgement, we thought it was our doom
[00:57.83] The radio reported, we listened with alarm
[01:04.52] The wild and windy actions of this great, mysterious storm
[01:11.33] From Albuquerque and Clovis and all New Mexico
[01:18.11] They said it was the blackest that ever they had saw
[01:24.84] From old Dodge City, Kansas, the dust had rung their knell
